!-----------------------------------------------------------------------
!
! Absorption cross-section CF2ClBr (HA1211): CF2ClBr + hv --> Br + Cl
! source : JPL-2006 (no change with respect to JPL-2002)
! http://www.atmosphere.mpg.de/enid/2295
! -> Catalogue -> "Halogeno-alkanes, -alkyl radicals" -> "Halons(C,H,F,Cl,Br)" 
!           -> "CF2ClBr(Halon-1211)" -> "JPL-2002"
! Rem1: Quantum yield = 1. However, JPL-2006 reports nonunity values of q.y. at some wl.
!   Since they are not useful for our purpose (too few wl are considered),
!   we fix q.y. to unity.
! Rem2: Temperature influence:
!   i)  170-200nm: T ind.
!   ii) 200-302nm: T dep. according to the formula (Gillotay & Simon, 1988):
!           log10 crs = sum An*wl^n + (T-273)*sum Bn*wl^n
!       where An and Bn are parameters introduced in CRS_CFC.
!       The cross sections are computed in subroutine CRS_TDEP. 
!       Accordingly, data (200-302nm) given below are not used.
! Rem3: JPL-2006 reports crs for wl > 302nm at room temperature (295-298K) without
!       mentioning their temperature dependence. According to Gillotay & Simon (1988),
!       crs depends strongly in temperature in the wl range.
!       Thus, they are not used here.
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Begins at wl interval :        44  | Finishes at wl interval :   92
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
!  no  from(nm) to(nm)  | crs (cm2) | qyield (0->1) |   Tdep_param1 |   Tdep_param2
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
